  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Transient upper level ridge continues \nto progress thru the western U.S. this morning with the ridge axis\nsituated over Nevada by sunrise. Will maintain patchy freezing \nfog within portions of the forecast area this morning and tomorrow\nmorning with satellite imagery already indicating freezing fog \nwithin portions of eastern Elko County this morning as of 110 AM \nPST. Otherwise weather will be fair today with high level clouds \ncontinuing to move in from the west with cloud bases concurrently\nlowering thru the day. This is thanks to a deep closed upper low \nsituated off shore of British Columbia and the associated \nmoisture plume streaming into the western U.S. A shortwave \nejecting from the broader circulation around the upper low passes \nthru Nevada Wednesday though no significant weather effects are \nexpected and dry weather looks to continue. However, will note a \nlow chance (10%) for a light shower or two across the high terrain\nof northern Nevada, north of the I-80 corridor. The latter half \nof the week will see high pressure establish itself offshore of \nSoCal. This will keep generally zonal flow over the Great Basin \nand the storm track pushed to the north with activity relegated to\nthe PacNW and western Canada. This keeps fair weather in place \nthru Friday under a warming trend. By Friday, daytime high \ntemperatures look to reside in the upper 40s to upper 50s, running\naround ten degrees warmer than normal for this time of year. \n\nA bit of discrepancy present among numerical model solutions this\nweekend with regard to chances of precipitaton. Some solutions \ndepict precipitation returning as early as Friday evening in \nnorthern Nevada as a shortwave moving in from the northwest \ndisplaces the region of high pressure situated offshore of SoCal. \nOther solutions maintain high pressure offshore thru Saturday. \nThat said, there seems to be relative agreement in at least light\nprecipitation moving in form the west in the Sunday time frame, \nthough accumulations look quite modest at this time. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Confidence is high with regard\nto warmer than average temperatures and fair weather thru Friday.\nConfidence is moderate pertaining to increasing probability of\nprecipitaton this weekend. Minimal deviations from NBM/WPC \nforecast.",
